# {{ service_name }}

{{ description }}. Made from `worker-template` (Copier); `.copier-answers.yml` records the version.

## Commands
```sh
uv sync
uv run ruff check && uv run ruff format --check && uv run mypy && uv run pytest
uv run alembic upgrade head
uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "<message>"
uv run taskiq worker app.core.broker:broker --fs-discover --tasks-pattern "app/**/tasks.py"
uv run python -m scripts.send_ping     # send a ping task to a running worker
docker build -t {{ service_name }}:local .
copier update --trust                  # pull template changes; commit first
```
Tests need Postgres (CI: a `postgres:18` service; locally, the api repo's `compose.dev.yml` stack). They recreate a `{{ domain }}_test` database.

## Layout
- `app/core/`: settings, broker, database, the declarative `Base`.
- `app/health/`: the `{{ domain }}.ping.v1` task. Entry points always live in `app/**/tasks.py`.
{%- if use_s3 %}
- `app/storage/`: S3 client.
{%- endif %}

## Contracts
- **Owns** the `{{ domain }}` schema. Every table lives in it (`Base` sets the schema), and Alembic only looks at it.
- Task names are `{{ domain }}.<name>.v<n>`. A contract changes by adding a version, never by editing one in place.

## Gotchas
- Import every models module in `migrations/env.py`, or autogenerate and `alembic check` won't see its tables.
- mypy is strict and covers `app`, `tests`, `migrations`, `scripts`.
